$quad$ #emph[\(a)]

#emph[\(b)] For any $A in frak(g)$, consider $gamma : bb(R) arrow.r frak(g)\,t mapsto t A$ which is a one parameter subgroup of $frak(g)$, thus $A = gamma'\(0\)in T_0 frak(g)$, and $exp A = gamma\(1\)= A$

#emph[\(c)] Define $gamma\(t\)= phi.alt\(exp t A\)$ which is a one parameter subgroup of $H$ since $gamma\(t + s\)= phi.alt\(exp\(t + s\)A\)= phi.alt\(exp t A exp s A\)= phi.alt\(exp t A\)phi.alt\(exp s A\)= gamma\(t\)gamma\(s\)$, then $gamma'\(0\)= frac(partial, partial t)\|_(t = 0) phi.alt\(exp t A\)=\(d phi.alt\)_1 frac(partial, partial t)\|_(t = 0) exp t A =\(d phi.alt\)_1 A$, on the other hand, $exp\(t\(d phi.alt\)_1 A\)$ is one parameter subgroup of $H$ corresponds to $\(d phi.alt\)_1 A = gamma'\(0\)$, thus $exp\(t\(d phi.alt\)_1 A\)= gamma\(t\)= phi.alt\(exp t A\)$

]
#statement("Proposition")[
Let $G$ be a Lie group and $H lt.eq G$ a Lie subgroup, then $"Lie"\(H\)= {A in "Lie" \( G \) mid(bar.v) exp t A in H \, forall t in bb(R)}$

]
